{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]You traded nails for my destiny
[F]Your great sacrifice has set me free
[C]And in my weakness You carried me
[F]You pulled me out of my bed of complacency
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
You [Am7]set me in heavenly places
[F2]Set me in heavenly places
[C/E]Here in Your kindness and in Your [Gsus]love
You [Am7]set me in heavenly places
[F2]Set me in heavenly places
[C/E]I'm finally home now and I [Gsus]see that God You are enough
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Now I'm standing before the throne
[F]I behold You and see I'm not my own
[C]Here in Your glory and in Your grace
[F]I'm overcome by the love that's on Your face
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [G]You raised me up
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [G]You raised me up
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [G]You raised me up
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [G]You raised me up
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
You [Am]set me in heavenly [G/B]places
[C]Set me in heavenly [Dm]places
[F]Here in Your kindness and [Am]in Your [Gsus]love
You [Am]set me in heavenly [G/B]places
[C]Set me in heavenly [Dm]places
[F]Here in Your kindness and [Am]in Your [Gsus]love
You [Am]set me in heavenly [G/B]places
[C]Set me in heavenly [Dm]places
[F]I'm finally home now [Am]and I [Gsus]see that God You are enough
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge 2}
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [Gsus]You raised me up
[Am7] [F2] [C/E] [Gsus]You raised me up
{end_of_bridge}
